    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d861">

                <pb facs="0789" n="617" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg617"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 701.6211/450</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Swiss Chargé</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hübscher</hi>)</head>
                <p>The Secretary of State presents his compliments to the Chargé d’Affaires <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ad interim</hi> of Switzerland, in charge of German
                    interests in the United States, and referring to the memorandum of the <pb
                        facs="0790" n="618" xml:id="pg618"/> Swiss Legation dated April 25, 1918,
                    has the honor to say that the proposal made that the Spanish Vice Consul at
                    Panama, in charge of German interests in the Republic of Panama, shall also be
                    allowed to assume protection of German interests in the Canal Zone is agreeable
                    to the Government of the United States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-24"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">August 24, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
